Why Is Demand Increasing
Rising demand for advanced rehabilitation: Increasing demand for functional restoration following limb loss is encouraging the development of prosthetics with improved movement, control, and comfort.
Technological innovation: Sensors, microprocessors, robotics, and myoelectric control are improving the responsiveness and usability of advanced prosthetic devices.
Expanding rehabilitation services: Greater investment in rehabilitation infrastructure and prosthetic care is creating opportunities for manufacturers and service providers.

Robotic Prosthetics Market Watch: AI-Assisted Control and Bionic Mobility
Robotic prosthetics are evolving through improvements in sensor integration, machine learning, and control systems that interpret muscle signals or other user inputs. These developments aim to improve movement coordination, adaptability, and user experience. Research into neural interfaces and advanced feedback mechanisms is also expanding the possibilities for upper- and lower-limb prosthetic applications.

